{% comment %}
  SHEmakes — the header.

  Built, not restyled. Five categories with a dropdown under each, replacing a
  three-level mega-menu — the change the whole redesign turns on.

  The menu is a real Shopify menu (Navigation → Menus). A top-level link with
  children becomes a category; its children open beneath it. One level deep on
  purpose: any third level is ignored rather than rendered, so the mega-menu
  cannot grow back through the admin.

  The dropdown opens on hover and on focus, so it is reachable from a keyboard.
  No JavaScript — CSS :hover and :focus-within do both.
{% endcomment %}

{%- liquid
  assign menu = linklists[section.settings.menu]

  comment
    A menu typed into the theme, one block per top-level item. The shop wanted
    eight specific entries out of a menu it also uses elsewhere, which no
    amount of hiding gets to. Blocks present means the Shopify menu below is
    not read at all.
  endcomment
  assign nav_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'nav'

  comment
    Two adjustments the theme can make to a Shopify menu without anyone editing
    the menu itself: drop entries by title, and add one link of the shop's own.

    The shop wanted "ALL Collections - DTF" — a category with twenty-three
    children nobody reads — replaced by a single "Ready to Press Transfers"
    link to the collections page, which now groups those same collections. Both
    are settings, so the menu in the admin stays as it is and this stays
    reversible.
  endcomment
  assign hidden_titles = section.settings.hide_titles | default: '' | downcase
  assign hidden_blob = hidden_titles | replace: ', ', ',' | prepend: ',' | append: ','

  assign extra_label = section.settings.extra_label
  assign extra_after = section.settings.extra_after | downcase | strip

  comment
    Count what will actually be in the bar before deciding what spills into
    "More": hiding one link and adding another both move that line.
  endcomment
  assign visible_count = 0
  for link in menu.links
    assign candidate = link.title | downcase | strip | prepend: ',' | append: ','
    unless hidden_blob contains candidate
      assign visible_count = visible_count | plus: 1
    endunless
  endfor
  if extra_label != blank
    assign visible_count = visible_count | plus: 1
  endif

  if nav_blocks.size > 0
    assign visible_count = nav_blocks.size
  endif

  assign shown = section.settings.max_categories | default: 5
  assign overflow = visible_count | minus: shown

  comment
    With one link left over, "More" costs as much room as the link itself.
  endcomment
  if overflow == 1
    assign shown = shown | plus: 1
    assign overflow = 0
  endif
-%}

<header class="sm-header" style="--sm-logo-height: {{ section.settings.logo_height | default: 48 }}px">
  <div class="sm-container sm-header__inner">
    <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="sm-header__logo" aria-label="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
      {%- if section.settings.logo -%}
        <img
          src="{{ section.settings.logo | image_url: width: 300 }}"
          alt="{{ shop.name | escape }}"
          width="{{ section.settings.logo.width }}"
          height="{{ section.settings.logo.height }}"
          loading="eager"
        >
      {%- else -%}
        <span class="sm-header__wordmark">{{ shop.name }}</span>
      {%- endif -%}
    </a>

    <nav class="sm-header__nav" aria-label="Main">
      <ul role="list">
        {%- if nav_blocks.size > 0 -%}
          {%- for block in nav_blocks -%}
            {%- if forloop.index > shown -%}{%- break -%}{%- endif -%}

            {%- comment -%}
              Children are one "Label | /url" per line, parsed the way the
              footer parses its columns. Blank stays an empty array rather
              than a one-element one, or every item grows an empty dropdown.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- assign kids = '' | split: ',' -%}
            {%- if block.settings.children != blank -%}
              {%- assign kids = block.settings.children | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
            {%- endif -%}

            <li class="sm-header__item{% if kids.size > 0 %} sm-header__item--has-menu{% endif %}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <a
                href="{{ block.settings.url | default: routes.root_url }}"
                class="sm-header__link{% if request.path == block.settings.url %} is-active{% endif %}"
              >
                {{ block.settings.label }}

                {%- if kids.size > 0 -%}
                  <svg class="sm-header__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                    <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
                  </svg>
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>

              {%- if kids.size > 0 -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A menu the length of the shop's own — twenty-three DTF
                  themes, seventeen UV ones — is a column of links taller than
                  the window. Past eight it is set in columns instead, and the
                  panel is centred under its item so neither edge of the page
                  cuts it off.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A line that starts with a dash is a child of the line above
                  it, and a menu with any of those is drawn as columns with
                  their own headings — the shop's UV DTF menu is three levels
                  deep and the third was being dropped on the floor.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- assign grouped = false -%}
                {%- for row in kids -%}
                  {%- assign mark = row | strip | slice: 0 -%}
                  {%- if mark == '-' -%}
                    {%- assign grouped = true -%}
                    {%- break -%}
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}

                <div class="sm-header__dropdown{% if grouped %} sm-header__dropdown--wide{% endif %}">
                  {%- if grouped -%}
                    <div class="sm-header__columns">
                      {%- assign group_open = false -%}
                      {%- assign list_open = false -%}
                      {%- for row in kids -%}
                        {%- assign line = row | strip -%}
                        {%- if line == blank -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

                        {%- assign is_child = false -%}
                        {%- assign mark = line | slice: 0 -%}
                        {%- if mark == '-' -%}
                          {%- assign is_child = true -%}
                          {%- assign line = line | remove_first: '-' | strip -%}
                        {%- endif -%}

                        {%- assign parts = line | split: '|' -%}
                        {%- assign label = parts[0] | strip -%}
                        {%- assign url = parts[1] | default: '#' | strip -%}

                        {%- if is_child -%}
                          {%- unless list_open -%}<ul role="list">{%- assign list_open = true -%}{%- endunless -%}
                          <li><a href="{{ url }}">{{ label }}</a></li>
                        {%- else -%}
                          {%- if list_open -%}</ul>{%- assign list_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}
                          {%- if group_open -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
                          <div class="sm-header__group">
                            <a class="sm-header__group-title" href="{{ url }}">{{ label }}</a>
                          {%- assign group_open = true -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                      {%- if list_open -%}</ul>{%- endif -%}
                      {%- if group_open -%}</div>{%- endif -%}
                    </div>
                  {%- else -%}
                    <ul role="list">
                      {%- for row in kids -%}
                        {%- assign parts = row | strip | split: '|' -%}
                        {%- if parts.size > 1 -%}
                          <li><a href="{{ parts[1] | strip }}">{{ parts[0] | strip }}</a></li>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </ul>
                  {%- endif -%}
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
            </li>
          {%- endfor -%}
        {%- else -%}
        {%- assign position = 0 -%}
        {%- for link in menu.links -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign title_key = link.title | downcase | strip | prepend: ',' | append: ','
            assign is_hidden = false
            if hidden_blob contains title_key
              assign is_hidden = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- if is_hidden -%}
            {%- continue -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            Anything past the category limit moves into "More" below rather
            than off the edge of the bar. The shop's menu has long labels;
            left alone the last one was cut in half.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- if position > shown -%}
            {%- break -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- assign is_active = false -%}
          {%- if link.active or link.child_active -%}
            {%- assign is_active = true -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- liquid
            comment
              Where a category's children live.

              The shop's own menus carry the nesting: `main-menu` is flat, and
              each category has a menu of its own named after it — which is how
              the old theme drew its mega-menu. Reading both means the sub-links
              the shop already maintains appear here without anyone re-entering
              them.
            endcomment
            assign children = link.links
            if children.size == 0
              assign handled = link.title | handleize
              assign children = linklists[handled].links
            endif
          -%}

          <li class="sm-header__item{% if children.size > 0 %} sm-header__item--has-menu{% endif %}">
            <a
              href="{{ link.url }}"
              class="sm-header__link{% if is_active %} is-active{% endif %}"
              {% if is_active %}aria-current="page"{% endif %}
            >
              {{ link.title }}

              {%- if children.size > 0 -%}
                <svg class="sm-header__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
                </svg>
              {%- endif -%}
            </a>

            {%- if children.size > 0 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                A child with children of its own becomes a column with its own
                heading — the shop's UV DTF menu is three levels deep, and the
                third level was being dropped on the floor.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {%- assign has_columns = false -%}
              {%- for child in children -%}
                {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                  {%- assign has_columns = true -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              {%- endfor -%}

              <div class="sm-header__dropdown{% if has_columns %} sm-header__dropdown--wide{% endif %}">
                {%- if has_columns -%}
                  <div class="sm-header__columns">
                    {%- for child in children -%}
                      <div class="sm-header__group">
                        <a class="sm-header__group-title" href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a>

                        {%- if child.links.size > 0 -%}
                          <ul role="list">
                            {%- for grandchild in child.links -%}
                              <li><a href="{{ grandchild.url }}">{{ grandchild.title }}</a></li>
                            {%- endfor -%}
                          </ul>
                        {%- endif -%}
                      </div>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </div>
                {%- else -%}
                  <ul role="list">
                    {%- for child in children -%}
                      <li>
                        <a href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a>
                      </li>
                    {%- endfor -%}
                  </ul>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          </li>

          {%- liquid
            assign follows = link.title | downcase | strip
            assign show_extra = false
            if extra_label != blank and follows == extra_after
              assign show_extra = true
            endif
          -%}

          {%- if show_extra -%}
            {%- assign position = position | plus: 1 -%}
            <li class="sm-header__item">
              <a
                href="{{ section.settings.extra_url | default: routes.collections_url }}"
                class="sm-header__link{% if request.path == section.settings.extra_url %} is-active{% endif %}"
              >
                {{ extra_label }}
              </a>
            </li>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
        {%- endif -%}

        {%- if overflow > 0 -%}
          <li class="sm-header__item sm-header__item--has-menu">
            <a href="{{ routes.root_url }}" class="sm-header__link">
              {{ section.settings.more_label }}
              <svg class="sm-header__chevron" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="m6 9 6 6 6-6"/>
              </svg>
            </a>

            <div class="sm-header__dropdown">
              <ul role="list">
                {%- if nav_blocks.size > 0 -%}
                  {%- for block in nav_blocks -%}
                    {%- if forloop.index <= shown -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}
                    <li><a href="{{ block.settings.url | default: routes.root_url }}">{{ block.settings.label }}</a></li>
                  {%- endfor -%}
                {%- else -%}
                {%- assign counted = 0 -%}
                {%- for link in menu.links -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign title_key = link.title | downcase | strip | prepend: ',' | append: ','
                    assign is_hidden = false
                    if hidden_blob contains title_key
                      assign is_hidden = true
                    endif
                  -%}

                  {%- if is_hidden -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

                  {%- assign counted = counted | plus: 1 -%}
                  {%- if counted <= shown -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

                  <li><a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.title }}</a></li>
                {%- endfor -%}
                {%- endif -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          </li>
        {%- endif -%}
      </ul>
    </nav>

    {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
      {%- capture search_props -%}
{
  "action": {{ routes.search_url | json }},
  "placeholder": {{ section.settings.search_placeholder | default: 'Search designs, sizes…' | json }},
  "value": {{ search.terms | default: '' | json }},
  "currency": {{ cart.currency.iso_code | json }}
}
      {%- endcapture -%}

      {%- capture search_fallback -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          The plain GET form. React adds the results-as-you-type dropdown on
          top of it; without the bundle this still searches the shop.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <form action="{{ routes.search_url }}" method="get" role="search" class="sm-header__search">
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="sm-search">Search</label>
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"/>
          </svg>
          <input
            id="sm-search"
            type="search"
            name="q"
            placeholder="{{ section.settings.search_placeholder | default: 'Search designs, sizes…' }}"
            value="{{ search.terms | escape }}"
          >
        </form>
      {%- endcapture -%}

      <div class="sm-header__searchbox">
        {% render 'sm-island', name: 'search', props: search_props, fallback: search_fallback %}
      </div>
    {%- endif -%}

    <div class="sm-header__actions">

      {%- comment -%}
        On a phone the bar reads the way the shop asked for: menu and search on
        the left, the logo centred, account and bag on the right. The order is
        CSS, so the desktop bar is untouched — see `.sm-header__inner` in
        shemakes.css.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if section.settings.show_search -%}
        <button type="button" class="sm-header__searchtoggle" data-sm-search-toggle aria-expanded="false">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m21 21-4.35-4.35"/>
          </svg>
          <span class="visually-hidden">Search</span>
        </button>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- if shop.customer_accounts_enabled -%}
        <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}" class="sm-header__account" aria-label="Account">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="8" r="4"/><path d="M4 21c0-4.42 3.58-7 8-7s8 2.58 8 7"/>
          </svg>
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      <a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}" class="sm-header__cart" data-sm-cart-open aria-label="Cart, {{ cart.item_count }} items">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M2.95 20c0 1.1.9 2 2 2h14c1.1 0 2-.9 2-2V7c0-.16-.05-.31-.11-.44s-1.72-3.45-1.72-3.45A2 2 0 0 0 17.33 2H6.56c-.76 0-1.45.42-1.79 1.11L3.05 6.56c-.07.14-.11.29-.11.45v13ZM12 15c-2.76 0-5-2.24-5-5h2c0 1.65 1.35 3 3 3s3-1.35 3-3h2c0 2.76-2.24 5-5 5M6.56 4h10.76l1 2H5.56z"/>
        </svg>
        {%- comment -%}
          Always rendered, hidden at zero: the count is updated in place by
          shemakes.js when the cart changes, and it cannot update an element
          that Liquid decided not to print.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        <span class="sm-header__count" data-sm-cart-count {% if cart.item_count == 0 %}hidden{% endif %}>
          {{- cart.item_count -}}
        </span>
      </a>

      {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
        <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url | default: '#' }}" class="sm-button sm-button--primary sm-header__cta">
          {{ section.settings.cta_label }}
        </a>
      {%- endif -%}

      {%- comment -%}
        The mobile panel is a <details>, so it opens without JavaScript and
        closes on Escape for free.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      <details class="sm-header__mobile">
        <summary aria-label="Menu">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true">
            <path d="M4 6h16"/><path d="M4 12h16"/><path d="M4 18h16"/>
          </svg>
        </summary>

        <div class="sm-header__panel">
          {%- comment -%}
            The two controls that live in the bar on a desktop and are simply
            not in the bar on a phone: the account link, and the button the
            whole shop turns on. The hamburger is the only place left for
            them, so it carries them at the top rather than leaving a shopper
            to find the custom order page through the menu.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <div class="sm-header__panel-top">
            {%- if section.settings.cta_label != blank -%}
              <a href="{{ section.settings.cta_url | default: '#' }}" class="sm-button sm-button--primary sm-header__panel-cta">
                {{ section.settings.cta_label }}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}

            <a href="{{ routes.account_url }}" class="sm-header__panel-account">
              <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                <path d="M20 21v-2a4 4 0 0 0-4-4H8a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v2"/><circle cx="12" cy="7" r="4"/>
              </svg>
              {% if customer %}{{ customer.first_name | default: 'Account' }}{% else %}Sign in{% endif %}
            </a>
          </div>

          {%- if nav_blocks.size > 0 -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              The panel lists every block, children and all: a phone scrolls,
              so nothing needs to spill into More the way the bar does.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            {%- for block in nav_blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.children == blank -%}
                <a href="{{ block.settings.url | default: routes.root_url }}" class="sm-header__panel-link">{{ block.settings.label }}</a>
              {%- else -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A category with children is a fold, not a link followed by
                  its whole list. Twenty-four collections under one heading
                  turned the menu into a page of its own, and the item a
                  shopper wanted was three screens down.

                  The heading still goes somewhere: the summary is the
                  category, and the first child is the link to all of it.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <details class="sm-header__panel-group">
                  <summary class="sm-header__panel-link">{{ block.settings.label }}</summary>
                {%- assign kids = block.settings.children | newline_to_br | split: '<br />' -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  Inside the fold a group heading and its children are both
                  just links — the dash that marks a child in the setting is
                  stripped rather than printed.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- comment -%}
                  A group heading with its own list under it ("Cup Wraps +
                  Decals" and its twenty themes) is a fold of its own, shut
                  until tapped: opened all at once the themes ran three
                  screens long. The first row inside is the group itself.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                <ul class="sm-header__panel-children" role="list">
                  {%- assign sub_open = false -%}
                  {%- for row in kids -%}
                    {%- assign line = row | strip -%}
                    {%- assign is_child = false -%}
                    {%- assign mark = line | slice: 0 -%}
                    {%- if mark == '-' -%}
                      {%- assign is_child = true -%}
                      {%- assign line = line | remove_first: '-' | strip -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {%- assign parts = line | split: '|' -%}
                    {%- if parts.size < 2 -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

                    {%- if is_child -%}
                      <li><a href="{{ parts[1] | strip }}">{{ parts[0] | strip }}</a></li>
                    {%- else -%}
                      {%- if sub_open -%}</ul></details></li>{%- assign sub_open = false -%}{%- endif -%}

                      {%- assign next_line = kids[forloop.index] | default: '' | strip -%}
                      {%- assign next_mark = next_line | slice: 0 -%}
                      {%- if next_mark == '-' -%}
                        <li class="sm-header__panel-subwrap">
                          <details class="sm-header__panel-sub">
                            <summary>{{ parts[0] | strip }}</summary>
                            <ul role="list">
                              <li class="sm-header__panel-all"><a href="{{ parts[1] | strip }}">Shop all {{ parts[0] | strip }}</a></li>
                        {%- assign sub_open = true -%}
                      {%- else -%}
                        <li class="sm-header__panel-group"><a href="{{ parts[1] | strip }}">{{ parts[0] | strip }}</a></li>
                      {%- endif -%}
                    {%- endif -%}
                  {%- endfor -%}
                  {%- if sub_open -%}</ul></details></li>{%- endif -%}
                </ul>
                </details>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          {%- else -%}
          {%- for link in menu.links -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign title_key = link.title | downcase | strip | prepend: ',' | append: ','
              assign is_hidden = false
              if hidden_blob contains title_key
                assign is_hidden = true
              endif
            -%}

            {%- if is_hidden -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endif -%}

            <a href="{{ link.url }}" class="sm-header__panel-link">{{ link.title }}</a>

            {%- if link.links.size > 0 -%}
              {%- comment -%}
                On a phone the categories are headings with their children
                listed under them — a dropdown inside a panel that is already a
                dropdown is the mega-menu all over again.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              <ul class="sm-header__panel-children" role="list">
                {%- for child in link.links -%}
                  <li><a href="{{ child.url }}">{{ child.title }}</a></li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endfor -%}
          {%- endif -%}

          {%- comment -%}
            The upsell row the shop asked for: opening the menu on a phone is
            the moment someone is deciding where to go, so the shortcut sits
            there rather than three taps further in.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          {%- liquid
            assign panel_collection = collections[section.settings.menu_collection]
            comment
              Nothing chosen still shows something worth tapping, rather than
              an empty strip at the bottom of every menu.
            endcomment
            if panel_collection == blank or panel_collection.products_count == 0
              assign panel_collection = collections.all
            endif
          -%}
          {%- if panel_collection.products_count > 0 -%}
            <div class="sm-header__promo">
              <p class="sm-eyebrow">{{ section.settings.menu_heading }}</p>

              <ul class="sm-header__promo-rail" role="list">
                {%- for product in panel_collection.products limit: section.settings.menu_count -%}
                  <li>
                    <a href="{{ product.url }}">
                      {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                        <img src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 300 }}" alt="" loading="lazy">
                      {%- else -%}
                        <span class="sm-card__placeholder"></span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      <span class="sm-header__promo-title">{{ product.title }}</span>
                      <span class="sm-header__promo-price">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
                    </a>
                  </li>
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SHEmakes header",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "logo", "label": "Logo" },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "logo_height",
      "label": "Logo height",
      "min": 28,
      "max": 72,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 48,
